{"name":"Saffron Desires","hex":"#c24359","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"saffron","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of species Crocus sativus, a crocus.","A spice (seasoning) and colouring agent made from the stigma and part of the style of the plant, sometimes or formerly also used as a dye and insect repellent."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an orange-yellow colour.","Associated with Hinduism, Hindus or Hindu nationalism."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/saffron"},{"term":"desires","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of desire"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of desire"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desires"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saffron","blocks":[{"text":"Saffron is a spice derived from the sterile autumn-blooming flower of Crocus sativus, commonly known as the \"saffron crocus\". The vivid crimson stigma and styles are collected and dried for use mainly as a food seasoning and colourant. Saffron crocus was slowly propagated throughout much of Eurasia and later brought to parts of North Africa, North America, even as far as Fiji in Oceania by its Indian migrant descendant population."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Saffron_-_premium_spice.jpg/330px-Saffron_-_premium_spice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saffron","wikidata":"Q25434"},{"title":"Desire","blocks":[{"text":"Desires are states of mind that are expressed by terms like \"wanting\", \"wishing\", \"longing\" or \"craving\". A great variety of features are commonly associated with desires. They are seen as propositional attitudes towards conceivable states of affairs. They represent how an agent or organism wills things to be, unlike beliefs, which aim to represent how things actually are. Desires are closely related to agency: they motivate the agent to realize them. For this to be possible, a desire has to be combined with a belief about which action would realize it. Desires present their objects in a favorable light, as something that appears to be good. Their fulfillment is normally experienced as pleasurable in contrast to the negative experience of failing to do so. Conscious desires are usually accompanied by some form of emotional response. While many researchers roughly agree on these general features, there is significant disagreement about how to define desires, i.e. which of these features are essential and which ones are merely accidental. Action-based theories define desires as structures that incline us toward actions. Pleasure-based theories focus on the tendency of desires to cause pleasure when fulfilled. Value-based theories identify desires with attitudes toward values, like judging or having an appearance that something is good."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Aristide_Maillol_-_D%C3%A9sir.jpg/330px-Aristide_Maillol_-_D%C3%A9sir.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desire","wikidata":"Q775842"},{"title":"Saffron (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Saffron is a shade of yellow or orange, the colour of the tip of the saffron crocus thread, from which the spice saffron is derived. The hue of the spice saffron is primarily due to the carotenoid chemical crocin."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saffron_(color)","wikidata":"Q2725283"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg/500px-Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg/1280px-Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg/500px-Saffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Corms","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaffron_onions-IMG_7549-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/500px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/960px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/500px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%A7%DB%8C_%D8%B3%D9%86%D9%88_-_%D9%85%D9%87%D8%AF%DB%8C_%D8%B0%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C_%2878%29.jpg/500px-%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%A7%DB%8C_%D8%B3%D9%86%D9%88_-_%D9%85%D9%87%D8%AF%DB%8C_%D8%B0%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C_%2878%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%A7%DB%8C_%D8%B3%D9%86%D9%88_-_%D9%85%D9%87%D8%AF%DB%8C_%D8%B0%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C_%2878%29.jpg/960px-%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%A7%DB%8C_%D8%B3%D9%86%D9%88_-_%D9%85%D9%87%D8%AF%DB%8C_%D8%B0%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%81%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%B1%DB%8C_%2878%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%AA%D8%A7%DB%8C_%